The '''clone Z-95 starfighter''', also known as the '''clone Z-95 Headhunter''' and more commonly known as the '''Headhunter starfighter''', was a model of [[starfighter]] and variant of the standard [[Z-95 Headhunter]] used by the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[clone trooper pilot]]s during the [[Clone Wars]]. Although not introduced until some time into the war, the clone Z-95 became one of the most popular forms of Republic air support. The versatile fighter saw action from the [[Battle of Umbara]] until the end of the war.

==Description==
[[File:CloneZ95HeadhunterDisplay-MF59.png|thumb|250px|left|The cockpit display in a clone Z-95 Headhunter]]
A joint venture between [[Incom Corporation|Incom]] and [[Sublights Products Corporation]], the clone [[Z-95 Headhunter]] was the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Republic Navy|naval forces']] primary multi-role [[starfighter]]. These Z-95 Headhunters were a 75,000-[[Galactic Credit Standard|credit]] starfighter designed specifically for the Navy to take advantage of the physical and mental capabilities of [[clone trooper pilot]]s. It was fast and agile, and while its [[proton torpedo launcher]]s armed with eight [[Proton torpedo|torpedoes]]<ref name="Rise" /> each gave the fighter a punch well out of proportion to its size of 16.74 [[meter]]s long and 18.13 meters wide.<ref name="DB Z95" /> The fighter was armed with [[Taim & Bak]] manufactured [[KX5 laser cannon]]s,<ref name="OWM" /> as well as close-ranged [[sensor]]s and a [[Standard day|day's]] worth of consumables.<ref name="Rise" /> The clone Z-95 also had a narrower fuselage than the standard Z-95 model.<ref name="SWEncyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref>

==History==
===Clone Wars===
[[File:BattleOverUmbara-DOU.png|thumb|left|250px|Z-95s escorting Republic forces to Umbara]]
The [[Republic Navy]] employed the Z-95 starfighter in several capacities, including escort and [[starfighter combat]] against enemy forces from the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|Navy]] of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. At the lengthy [[Battle of Umbara]], Z-95s fought as the Republic fleet broke through the Separatist blockade, and later provided escort to gunships that were deploying troops on the surface.<ref name="Darkness">{{TCW|Darkness on Umbara}}</ref> As the battle wore on, Z-95s combated [[Zenuas 33 Umbaran starfighter|Umbaran starfighters]] when the Republic engaged a Separatist fleet in space.<ref name="Plan of Dissent">{{TCW|Plan of Dissent}}</ref> [[Drift (clone trooper)|Drift]] flew a Z-95 in one engagement.<ref name="X-wing">{{Twitter|atomicmassgames|status/1521899696394051584|Atomic Mass Games|quote=Check out "Killer," "Drift," and "Stub" three Clone pilots joining the Republic in the Clone Z-95 Headhunter Expansion Pack for #StarWarsXWing. Pre-order your copy today! #StarWars #XWing #Miniatures|archivedate=20220504170924}}</ref>

[[File:CloneZ-95-EscapeKadavo.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Warthog's Z-95 during the battle]]
They would participate in the [[Battle of Kadavo]], where they provided escort to [[Jedi Master]] [[Plo Koon]] in his starfighter and [[104th Battalion]]'s [[Wolfpack]] gunships in a attempt to rescue [[Jedi General]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], and a group of [[Togruta]] slaves, who were being held captive by [[Zygerrian]] keeper [[Agruss]] in the [[Kadavo slave processing facility]]. During the battle, they engaged [[HH-87 Starhopper]]'s piloted by Zygerrian pilots, with clone pilot [[Warthog]]'s ship being damaged by one of them. Koon used his [[Plo Koon's Delta-7 Aethersprite-class light interceptor|starfighter]] to destroy both Starhoppers, saving Warthog and their fellow wingmen, but were unable to destroy the defense towers of the slave processing facility. However, with the help of [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], who was able to hijack one of the defense towers and destroy three of them, [[Admiral]] [[Barton Coburn]]'s ship, the ''[[Hand of Justice]]'', was able to get close to the facility and rescue the slaves before the gunships destroyed the facility.<ref name="Escape from Kadavo">{{TCW|Escape from Kadavo}}</ref>

During the [[Attack on Obi-Wan Kenobi's fleet|attack]] on Obi-Wan's [[Obi-Wan Kenobi's taskforce|fleet]], Z-95 Headhunters participated in defending the fleet from [[General]] [[Grievous]]. One Z-95 was piloted by clone pilot [[Killer]], who provided cover fire for his wingman [[Engle]], who was making bombing runs on [[Munificent-class star frigate|Separatist warships]] in his [[BTL Y-wing starfighter|Y-wing starfighter]]. Unfortunately, Killer was killed in the ensuing battle while Engle crash-landed on Kenobi's ship, the ''[[Negotiator]]''. Engle would escape the burning cockpit of his starfighter, with Kenobi helping him get to safety.<ref name="Rescue">{{TCW|Bound for Rescue}}</ref>

[[File:InterceptorsSoar-S.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Z-95s launching from a Republic cruiser]]
Z-95 Headhunters also participated in the [[Defense of Cato Neimoidia|defense]] of [[Cato Neimoidia]] where they were led by Anakin Skywalker and his [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] in an attempt to protect the planet from Separatist control. In the ensuing battle, Skywalker punched a hole against the [[Vulture-class starfighter|vulture droids]] to clear a path for the Z-95s and several of them engaged in dogfights against [[droid tri-fighter]]s, with one of them being shot down. Unfortunately, Skyalkwer and Tano were called off from the attack so they could investigate an [[Bombing at the Jedi Temple|attack on the Jedi Temple]], while the Republic continued the assault on the planet.<ref name="Sabotage">{{TCW|Sabotage (episode)}}</ref>

On Coruscant, a number of clone Z-95s were held as a reserve force in a [[Imperial Inspectorate HQ|Republic Navy base]], along with other starfighters and various personnel. Z-95s were also used as aerial security in [[Kamino]]'s cloning facilities, particularly at the [[clone military education complex]]. When Skywalker led a [[Battle of Ringo Vinda|campaign]] to free [[Ringo Vinda]] from [[Confederacy military|Separatist forces]], squadrons of Z-95 starfighters engaged the enemy fighters around the massive [[Ringo Vinda space station|space station]] orbiting the planet.<ref name="The Unknown">{{TCW|The Unknown}}</ref> During Skywalker's [[Invasion of Scipio|invasion]] of [[Scipio]], the headquarters of the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]], clone pilot [[Hawk]] and other pilots flew Z-95 starfighters as escort for the 501st Legion's [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry|LAAT/i gunships]]. Z-95s engaged vulture droids to clear a path for the gunships to land, allowing the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|Confederate navy]] to withdraw and abandon the ground forces left in the planet. In the ensuing chaos, Hawk and his comrades shot down the remaining vulture droids outside Scipio's [[Main Vault]], allowing the Republic to win the battle. However, one of the vulture droids shot down by Hawk crashed into the vault, inadvertently causing the death of [[Rush Clovis]], who was holding [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] hostage.<ref name="Crisis at the Heart">{{TCW|Crisis at the Heart}}</ref>

[[File:Battleforanaxes.png|thumb|right|250px|Z-95s during the Battle of Anaxes]]
Later, Z-95s participated in the [[Outer Rim Sieges]], where many of them engaged droid fighters at [[Anaxes]], home of the Republic Navy's shipyards, though many of them would result in heavy casualties.<ref name="The Bad Batch">{{TCW|The Bad Batch (episode)}}</ref> They further participated in a [[battle between a Republic and Separatist fleet]] led by [[Grievous]] and assisted [[Plo Koon]] in capturing [[Cato Neimoidia]]. Z-95s and Republic gunships also participated in the [[Battle of Yerbana]], where they engaged droid tri-fighters while Kenobi, [[Commander]] [[Cody]], and the [[212th Attack Battalion]] engaged the forces on the ground. Although some Z-95s were not as successful in shooting down the tri-fighters, the battle was still won by the Republic.<ref name="Old Friends Not Forgotten">{{TCW|Old Friends Not Forgotten}}</ref>

Z-95s were parked in a [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]] commanded by Skywalker near the end of the war. When Republic forces were called to [[Coruscant]] to respond to an [[Battle of Coruscant|planet invasion]], Skywalker was reunited with his former Padawan<ref name="Old Friends Not Forgotten" /> after Tano had left the [[Jedi Order]],<ref name="The Wrong Jedi">{{TCW|The Wrong Jedi}}</ref> in the hangar. When Tano was called off to [[Mandalore]] along with the rest of the newly formed [[332nd Company]] of the 501st Legion led by the newly promoted Commander Rex, [[Captain]] [[Vaughn]], [[Mandalore resistance|Mandalorian resistance forces]] led by [[Bo-Katan Kryze]], Skywalker, and Kenobi left for Coruscant.<ref name="Old Friends Not Forgotten" />

Not long after, Z-95 Headhunters were also parked aboard<ref name="Victory and Death">{{TCW|Victory and Death}}</ref> the ''[[Tribunal]]'',<ref name="TCW Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Character Encyclopedia - Join the Battle!]]''</ref> a ''Venator'' that had recently detained the former [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] following the [[Siege of Mandalore]]. When [[Order 66]] was [[Skirmish aboard the Tribunal|issued]], the [[332nd Division]] turned on Tano. After she had freed Rex from his [[Behavioral modification biochip|inhibitor chip]],<ref name="Shattered">{{TCW|Shattered}}</ref> the two passed by the Headhunters in the starship's repair bay while searching for a working ship to steal, eventually taking a [[BTL-B Y-wing starfighter/bomber]]. The Headhunters were all destroyed when the ''Tribunal'' crashed into a [[Unidentified moon|moon]].<ref name="Victory and Death" />

===Later use===
Between [[32 ABY]] and [[34 ABY]], one Z-95 Headhunter was piloted by [[Poe Dameron]] of the [[Resistance]]'s [[Black Squadron (Resistance)|Black Squadron]] during a [[Heist of the Alderaanian data archive|mission]] to obtain a [[Archive of the Great Library of Alderaan|data archive]] containing all that was left of the [[Royal Library of Alderaan|Royal Library]] of [[Alderaan]].<ref name="Poe Dameron Annual 2">[[Poe Dameron Annual 2|''Poe Dameron Annual'' 2]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|A multi-purpose starfighter, the Z-95 has spawned countless variants, with the Republic making its own mark on the Headhunter's large production run with a clone trooper-specific model.|StarWars.com Encyclopedia entry for the clone Z-95 starfighter|<ref name="Encyclopedia" />}}
[[File:CloneZ-95Design-DoU.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Concept art for the Z-95 starfighter model]]
The clone Z-95 Headhunter was developed for the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series and was first appeared in the episode "[[Darkness on Umbara]]" which aired in [[October]] [[2011]].<ref name="Darkness" /> The [http://www.starwars.com/explore/the-clone-wars/ep407/#!/about episode guide] for "Darkness on Umbara" on [[StarWars.com]] initially designated the craft as the "Z-85 Headhunter," implying that it was the predecessor of the Z-95 Headhunter, but this was later changed to "Headhunter starfighter." The starfighter's [http://www.starwars.com/explore/encyclopedia/technology/z95headhunter entry] in the [[Encyclopedia (StarWars.com)|StarWars.com Encyclopedia]] and later the Databank referred to it as a "Clone Z-95 starfighter" and clarified that it was one of many variants in Headhunter line.<ref name="Encyclopedia" />

The starfighter was designed by the television series' crew with the intention of avoiding similarity to the [[T-65 X-wing starfighter/Legends|T-65 X-wing starfighter]] from the [[original trilogy]] of ''[[Star Wars]]'' films. Instead, it more resembled artist [[Colin Cantwell]]'s original model for the X-wing starfighter.<ref name="Explore: Plan of Dissent">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/plan-of-dissent-episode-guide|text="Plan of Dissent" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

